+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling It Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 as confirmed by [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08: a booked visit was immutable, and both correction and cancellation sat outside the sample. That ADR set the terms on which the row could move — "narrowing either row later is a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR" — and a request alone was never enough to reopen it.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-23). A visit booked with the wrong date or a mistyped description cannot be put right, and the sample's own framing is what makes this awkward: it demonstrates forward-only correction for owners and pets, and stops one record short of the same pattern for visits.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the correction gap is the one place the forward-only pattern the sample teaches is visibly incomplete.
+2. **Open NG-5 entirely.** Build correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is a lifecycle transition — a visit that exists but did not happen — and the sample carries lifecycle state nowhere else. The 2026-08-08 rationale holds for it unchanged.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as `REQ-VIS-003`. Cancelling a booked visit remains out of scope and remains the whole of NG-5. Deleting a visit remains covered by NG-4, which this decision does not touch.
+
+Correction is a value change on an existing record: the visit keeps its identity and the pet's set of visits is unchanged in size. Any behavior that would remove a visit, or mark one as not-having-happened, is out.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The forward-only correction pattern now covers all three record types the sample writes: owner, pet, and visit.
+- NG-5 is narrower and no longer names "changing"; a future request to cancel a visit still needs its own recorded owner decision.
+- The future-date rule applies to every submission of the visit form, so a visit whose date has passed cannot be saved unchanged. Recorded as an edge case and an open question against `REQ-VIS-003`.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
